{"name":"Flintstone","hex":"#677283","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Flintstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in Central Highlands Council, central Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Flintstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flint","blocks":[{"text":"Flint, occasionally flintstone (SiO2), is a sedimentary cryptocrystalline form of the mineral quartz, categorized as the variety of chert that occurs in chalk or marly limestone. Historically, flint was widely used to make stone tools and start fires."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Miorcani_flint.jpg/330px-Miorcani_flint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flint"},{"title":"Flintstone, Georgia","blocks":[{"text":"Flintstone is an unincorporated community in Walker County, Georgia, United States. Located in northwestern Georgia, Flintstone lies approximately 12 miles south of Chattanooga, Tennessee, 120 miles northwest of Atlanta, 135 miles southeast of Nashville, Tennessee, and 150 miles northeast of Birmingham, Alabama. Although Flintstone is unincorporated, it has a post office, with the ZIP code of 30725; the ZCTA for ZIP Code 30725 had a population of 3,456 at the 2000 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Edged.jpg/330px-Edged.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flintstone%2C_Georgia"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg/500px-Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg/1280px-Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg/500px-Flint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A piece of flint 9–10 cm (3.5–3.9 in) long, weighing 171 grams","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlint%2C_9cm%2C_171gm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg/500px-Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg/1280px-Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg/500px-Silica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silicified remains of algae and silica pseudomorph after halite in flint. Pebble of Loire near Marcigny, France. Image width: about 5 mm","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilica_pseudomorph_after_halite_crystals_and_silicified_remains_of_algae_6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Flintbeach.jpg/250px-Flintbeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/Flintbeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Flintbeach.jpg/250px-Flintbeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pebble beach 